comments.body:
Implementation checkpoint is ready for the bootstrap push.

Landed in the working tree:
- neutral namespaced APIs and repository-owned composition function;
- rotating administrator and telemetry token chains;
- configurable ProviderConfig, SecretStore, and output-prefix seams;
- optional SSO, reports, plugins, incident relay, and custom role bindings;
- Crossplane, ESO, AWS workload-identity, and Argo CD examples;
- one comprehensive public guide and inert catalog examples;
- pinned-action CI, signed multi-platform package publishing, and public-release safety scanning.

Local evidence:
- public-release scan passed;
- Go race tests passed with 88.1% statement coverage;
- go vet passed;
- YAML parsing and both Kustomize renders passed;
- shellcheck and actionlint passed;
- zizmor --pedantic reported no findings.

The first non-closing commit will bootstrap the GHCR package. After that workflow publishes and signs the package, the platform manifest will be changed from the temporary main tag to the exact digest, a digest-specific Cosign verification gate will be added, and the final commit will close this issue.

Expanded parity and customer-reference pass started after the package was made public.

Verified inputs:
- anonymous GHCR bearer-token access to the pinned OCI index returns HTTP 200 for both amd64 and arm64;
- validation and signed-package workflows for b51fe2f both passed;
- the original Terraform reference was compared at its current remote main revision;
- provider behavior is being checked against provider-grafana v2.13.0 and its generated Terraform provider v4.40.0 contract.

The active Terraform resource surface is already represented structurally: stack, administrator credential, external secret document, three dashboard/folder pairs, organization home preference, scheduled report, OAuth SSO ownership modes, synchronized teams, custom roles/assignments, four incident webhooks, and two alerting contact points.

This final pass will add the missing customer-facing depth:
- provider-specific OAuth and SAML profile patterns with secret references and ownership modes;
- reusable team access beyond the one-team/one-role example, including direct membership, external-group sync, preferences, custom roles, and fixed-role assignments;
- an authoritative folder/dashboard ACL API with basic-role and team examples;
- clear collision/ownership rules for whole-set permission and role-assignment resources;
- detailed equivalence, coverage, and extension matrices in the single README;
- additional inert examples and validation coverage.

No live stacks or source infrastructure will be imported, adopted, or changed.

Final publication checkpoint:

- resource-by-resource comparison against the current Terraform source is complete;
- hosted validation for 7c3a37b passed;
- the new function package published as a public amd64/arm64 OCI index at sha256:36aee084bda51e1bd909ee40ce8f2144808130472b30d5f77f8e41162d0e2e2f;
- anonymous bearer-token retrieval returns HTTP 200;
- Cosign verification passed for the exact main-branch publication workflow identity;
- local validation, race tests (88.1% coverage), vet, YAML/Kustomize rendering, shellcheck, actionlint, zizmor, public-data scan, and diff checks pass.

The final pin now points both the Function and the in-cluster verification hook at that immutable digest. The remaining action is the closing commit and its hosted validation.
